<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!-- The Skills module: the shared skill taxonomy, and nothing else.

       PROMOTED EARLY. The Phase 13 plan created this project at 13.3, alongside the
       schema split. It arrived at 13.2 instead because ISkillCatalog needs an owner
       now — four modules find-or-create against `skills` today, and parking the
       implementation inside Applications would mean moving the file again one step
       later, for no gain in between.

       Why `skills` is its own module at all: posting_skills (Applications) and
       resume_skills (Documents) point at the SAME row, so the table is co-owned in
       practice. That shared row is what the Phase 7 natural key and the Phase 5
       skill gap both turn on. A table two modules both need to write is not owned
       by either of them.

       It has no routes and no slices — the taxonomy is never asked for on its own,
       only resolved on the way to something else. If a "browse all skills" screen
       ever lands, this is where it goes.

       REFERENCE RULE, enforced by tests/Jobkeep.Tests/Architecture/: this project
       may reference SharedKernel, Contracts and (until 13.3) Infrastructure.Data.
       It may NOT reference another Jobkeep.Modules.* project. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Jobkeep.Modules.Skills</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../Jobkeep.SharedKernel/Jobkeep.SharedKernel.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../Jobkeep.Contracts/Jobkeep.Contracts.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../Jobkeep.Infrastructure.Data/Jobkeep.Infrastructure.Data.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
